			<item>
				<title>Java Friday Fun: @WTF annotations in code</title>
				<link>https://justaddwater.dk/2011/09/16/java-friday-fun-wtf-annotations-in-code/</link>
				<pubDate>Fri, 16 Sep 2011 21:52:08 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://justaddwater.dk/2011/09/16/java-friday-fun-wtf-annotations-in-code/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Time for a little geeky gimmick. Some developers see and express a lot of &amp;ldquo;WTF??&amp;rdquo; while trying to understand code&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2011/09/focus-shift-cartoon-wtf-per-minute-wtfm.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2011/09/focus-shift-cartoon-wtf-per-minute-wtfm-300x282.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;&#34; title=&#34;focus-shift-cartoon-wtf-per-minute-wtfm&#34; class=&#34;aligncenter size-medium wp-image-1493&#34; height=&#34;282&#34; width=&#34;300&#34; srcset=&#34;https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2011/09/focus-shift-cartoon-wtf-per-minute-wtfm-300x282.jpg 300w, https://justaddwater.dk/wp-content/uploads/2011/09/focus-shift-cartoon-wtf-per-minute-wtfm.jpg 500w&#34; sizes=&#34;(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;IN this spirit, i created a quick @WTF annotation for Java.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Besides being completely useless (its removed at compile time), its only purpose is to give developers a new way to express themselves in code.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;WTF.java — &lt;a href=&#34;https://gist.github.com/1222965&#34;&gt;gist on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-java&#34; data-lang=&#34;java&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;@Retention&lt;/span&gt;(RetentionPolicy.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;SOURCE&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;@Target&lt;/span&gt;({ElementType.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;TYPE&lt;/span&gt;, ElementType.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;FIELD&lt;/span&gt;, ElementType.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;METHOD&lt;/span&gt;, ElementType.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;CONSTRUCTOR&lt;/span&gt;, ElementType.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;LOCAL_VARIABLE&lt;/span&gt;})&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;@interface&lt;/span&gt; WTF {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;/**&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;     * Optionally specify &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;explain&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;, and write why you dont understand this annotated element&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;     */&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    String &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;explain&lt;/span&gt;() &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;/**&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;     * Optionally add &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;explanation&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt;, and to explain why and how the element should be used&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;     */&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;@Deprecated&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    String  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;explanation&lt;/span&gt;() &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The cartoon states &amp;ldquo;The only valid measurement of code quality: WTFs/minute&amp;rdquo;. With the &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;@WTF&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; annotations, I would like to take it a little further. By annotating the code, you can actually encourage colleagues to help you fix it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
